  "title": "First human heart transplant",
  "summary": "On the night of 2–3 December 1967, Christiaan Barnard led the team at Groote Schuur Hospital in Cape Town that gave Louis Washkansky the heart of Denise Darvall, a young woman fatally injured when struck by a car. Washkansky died of a severe lung infection on 21 December, the 18th day after surgery.",
